Subject: AOT: lean object lifecycle, lambda lifting, frameless-body helpers and the earleyboyer investigation knobs

What this does
  - Object lifecycle: a plain object freed while its fields are freed goes through a 32-entry free stack instead of the
    zero list (QJS_NOFREESTACK); a LIFO block cache in front of the arenas, accounted at push/pop (QJS_NOBLKCACHE,
    QJS_BLKCACHE_MAX); parking into a side array with the in_zct bit, and a parked object is not parked again
    (QJS_DRC_NOZARRAY, QJS_DRC_NOREPARK); a 2-deep pend ring holds a fresh object adopted into a register instead of
    parking it (js_drc_pend_flush runs at the start of a pin); the layout fields the generator needs to allocate a plain
    object inline (block cache, accounting, GC list, header image).
  - Construction: qjs_aot_new_fused / qjs_aot_fused_learn / qjs_aot_construct_learn allocate a field-only constructor's
    instance with its final shape; js_shape_try_hash enters an unhashed constructor shape into the shape table so the
    learning engages (every `new F()` of such a constructor took the slow path before).
  - Compiled-code helpers: qjs_aot_call_generic (a direct JS_CallInternal call of a callee the unit cannot enter
    natively), qjs_aot_make_closure / local_check / close_local / set_name (closure creation without the step engine),
    qjs_aot_instof_fill (inline instanceof caches, registered and released in JS_FreeRuntime).
  - Lambda lifting of local, call-only function expressions whose captured variables are not written after the closure
    is created (path-sensitive check), off by default (QJS_LIFT=1, QJS_LIFT_STATS=1).
  - js_arr_packed_num_int is called outside assert() in regvm_array_from_regs (it filled the packed buffer through
    the assert, so an NDEBUG build with packed arrays on produced zeros).
  - Measurement/validation knobs, off unless defined or set: QJS_DRC_STRESS_ALLOC (+QJS_DRC_STRESS_EVERY), QJS_DRC_STATS,
    SPL_COUNT, QJS_EXP_NOLIST, QJS_NEVERFREE, QJS_DRC_MINLIM, QJS_DRC_SLACK_MB, QJS_DEBUG_TPL, QJS_DEBUG_LEAK.

Why we need it
  The earleyboyer program (reviewer specs AOT-GAP-ROOT-CAUSE-2026-11-08.md and AOT-10X-PLAN-2026-11-08.md): object
  allocation and release in compiled code cost 374 instructions per object (18 ns vs node's 1 ns); these changes take
  the build.lit loop to 241 instructions/39 cycles per object and earleyboyer from 17.6k to about 21.5k on the Mac.

Soundness
  Every path keeps the deferred-counting invariant (a count-zero object is freed only at a reconcile, after the pin);
  ASan + a reconcile at every allocation ran clean on the repro set and earleyboyer.
